WEBVTT

01:30.480 --> 01:34.490
<b>Episode 9</b>

01:30.480 --> 01:34.490
<b>Earth Goes to the Fairy Kingdom</b>

01:42.820 --> 01:46.610
Hey, Earth, did you hear the 
news about the new ad campaign?

01:47.790 --> 01:50.540
Yeah, it's a big deal.

01:50.540 --> 01:52.290
Huh? What campaign?

01:52.290 --> 01:54.030
What? You don't know?

01:54.030 --> 01:57.730
There are four VR games out there right now.

01:58.470 --> 02:01.580
There's this game, <i>One More</i>, 
but also a fighting game,

02:02.970 --> 02:05.660
an FPS shooter,

02:06.680 --> 02:09.850
<b>"Launch a full-out assault!"</b>

02:07.050 --> 02:08.840
and a mech game.

02:10.450 --> 02:14.760
They all required their 
own specific VR helmet,

02:15.150 --> 02:20.120
but they all wanted more customers, 
so the publishers all worked together...

02:21.500 --> 02:24.700
And now you can play any game
with any of the helmets.

02:24.700 --> 02:26.010
I see.

02:26.290 --> 02:33.570
And so they're starting a big ad 
campaign for a 15-day free trial.

02:34.920 --> 02:41.210
And they'll be adding the Fairy Kingdom 
into <i>One More</i> on the first day it begins.

02:42.550 --> 02:48.020
All four games are going 
to get a lot more players.

02:49.270 --> 02:50.430
Ow!

02:50.430 --> 02:52.070
These are for the customers!

02:52.070 --> 02:55.250
I'll whack anybody who touches them, and that includes you, Zwei!

02:55.250 --> 02:56.950
You already whacked me!

02:57.300 --> 02:58.870
Oh, Nora...

02:59.400 --> 03:01.340
This is for you.

03:04.200 --> 03:06.920
This is so that if Zwei does something dumb,

03:06.920 --> 03:09.520
I can smack him hard, right?

03:10.560 --> 03:12.140
What was that for?!

03:13.830 --> 03:15.450
You've got it.

03:15.450 --> 03:16.510
Okay.

03:17.540 --> 03:20.480
If that many new players are coming,

03:20.480 --> 03:25.080
all the guilds must be getting 
ready to try to recruit them.

03:25.080 --> 03:27.780
Hey, put that thing away.

03:27.780 --> 03:30.880
Think we should start recruiting, too?

03:31.210 --> 03:35.230
I think we could be a good 
medium-sized guild, if we wanted to be.

03:35.510 --> 03:39.450
First, we'd have to make 
sure to get Eliza in line,

03:39.450 --> 03:41.910
or the new members 
might have a rough time.

03:41.910 --> 03:43.650
Eliza, huh?

03:50.820 --> 03:53.900
Earth saved her the other day, right?

03:56.160 --> 04:00.290
Listen, Earth, why don't 
you just join our guild?

04:03.530 --> 04:04.710
No.

04:04.710 --> 04:06.650
Why?

04:06.650 --> 04:09.360
I'm sorry I keep turning you 
down each time you ask.

04:11.510 --> 04:15.930
But, well... part of it is that 
I just want to do my own thing.

04:17.350 --> 04:21.580
<i>And there are some things I'd rather 
other players didn't find out about.</i>

04:22.190 --> 04:25.310
<i>The Queen and her sister, for instance...</i>

04:30.240 --> 04:32.470
A new item for your repertoire?

04:32.470 --> 04:35.720
Maybe I'll be the first to take a bite.

04:36.990 --> 04:39.140
This is something new 
I'm making for the customers.

04:39.140 --> 04:40.260
Don't eat it!

04:40.940 --> 04:42.950
You're mean.

04:42.950 --> 04:43.880
Who are you?

04:44.190 --> 04:49.060
You're telling me I have to look 
at this delicious meat and not eat it?

04:49.060 --> 04:50.960
Listen, Ryuu...

04:50.970 --> 04:52.140
Ryuu?

04:51.390 --> 04:54.830
If I let you start eating, 
you'll eat 15 of these steaks!

04:54.830 --> 04:56.420
You glutton!

04:56.420 --> 04:58.490
Who are you calling a glutton?

04:58.490 --> 05:00.340
It's true, isn't it?

05:00.340 --> 05:02.630
You'll regret saying that!

05:02.900 --> 05:04.810
Um...

05:05.840 --> 05:07.730
Who might you be?

05:08.060 --> 05:11.560
I've never seen an outfit 
like that before...

05:11.560 --> 05:12.750
Japanese clothes?

05:12.750 --> 05:16.160
And you don't look like a fairy.

05:17.580 --> 05:19.030
Oh...

05:20.510 --> 05:21.620
Earth!

05:21.620 --> 05:23.500
Don't tell me the queen 
wasn't enough for you,

05:23.500 --> 05:25.490
so you went after her, too?

05:25.490 --> 05:27.090
What?!

05:27.090 --> 05:28.400
I'm so jealous!

05:28.400 --> 05:29.430
I wish I could—

05:32.800 --> 05:35.100
Don't you start getting 
weird ideas, too, Rage!

05:35.100 --> 05:36.590
It's a compliment!

05:36.590 --> 05:37.800
Shaddup!

05:38.220 --> 05:41.780
She's practically eating 
me out of house and home!

05:41.780 --> 05:44.730
If I could give her to you, I would!

05:44.730 --> 05:46.930
They seem quite close.

05:44.730 --> 05:47.090
Can I eat this?

05:47.090 --> 05:50.630
Oh, fine...

05:47.950 --> 05:51.950
He called her "Ryuu," right?

05:53.160 --> 05:56.950
Indeed. Only Earth can call me that.

05:57.670 --> 06:00.720
I have no intention of 
letting anyone else do it.

06:02.070 --> 06:04.150
I'm putting this up on the game forum.

06:04.150 --> 06:08.170
If you do, I don't think 
I'll ever cook for you again.

06:09.000 --> 06:15.070
So first he's a fairy-playah, 
and now he's a dragon babysitter?

06:15.070 --> 06:16.890
He's taking an interesting path in life.

06:16.890 --> 06:17.930
Really.

06:18.890 --> 06:20.580
Give me a break, guys.

06:22.270 --> 06:26.360
<i>What would happen if I went to 
the Fairy Kingdom like this?</i>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Castle</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Town</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Town</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Town</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Town</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Fort</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>Fort</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>West</b>

06:26.780 --> 06:39.730
<b>East</b>

06:27.250 --> 06:31.990
<i>The Fairy Kingdom is south of 
the game's second city, Nexia.</i>

06:31.990 --> 06:35.200
<i>There's a castle at its center, 
with towns spreading out in a cross shape,</i>

06:35.200 --> 06:38.270
<i>and forts that serve as checkpoints 
in each cardinal direction.</i>

06:40.000 --> 06:44.270
<i>And today's the day it 
was put into the game!</i>

06:45.620 --> 06:50.090
<i>A ton of players are on 
their way there, of course.</i>

06:51.070 --> 06:54.170
<i>The usual way to get there is to walk.</i>

06:54.590 --> 06:56.980
<i>With so many people heading 
for the same place,</i>

06:56.980 --> 06:59.390
<i>it means everyone has something in common,</i>

06:59.390 --> 07:02.110
<i>and it's easy to talk with 
people you've never met.</i>

07:02.910 --> 07:05.320
So that's the north fortress?

07:05.320 --> 07:07.310
Oh, so that's the fort?

07:07.310 --> 07:09.310
We're finally here.

07:12.860 --> 07:15.750
It's huge...

07:22.050 --> 07:23.170
Um...

07:23.170 --> 07:24.040
Yes?

07:24.040 --> 07:28.670
If you don't mind, I'd like to take a closer 
look at that ring on your left hand.

07:29.030 --> 07:32.940
<i>Didn't she say something about 
this ring serving as a pass?</i>

07:33.250 --> 07:35.300
Oh, this?

07:37.070 --> 07:40.270
That's the Queen's ring, yes.

07:40.270 --> 07:42.670
So you're Earth.

07:42.670 --> 07:44.840
It is a pleasure to meet you.

07:44.840 --> 07:48.820
I am the leader of the northern fort.

07:48.820 --> 07:50.690
May I have a word?

07:50.690 --> 07:52.270
Is there something wrong?

07:52.270 --> 07:57.430
Her Highness has requested that you 
be brought to her immediately.

07:59.500 --> 08:01.900
Bring it here!

08:01.900 --> 08:02.620
Yes, sir!

08:02.620 --> 08:03.830
What's going on?

08:03.830 --> 08:05.310
An event?

08:06.530 --> 08:08.570
<i>Everyone's staring at me...</i>

08:21.710 --> 08:28.640
This is a pikasha, a bird which only a 
select few fairies are permitted to ride.

08:28.640 --> 08:30.990
It allows you to move very quickly.

08:30.990 --> 08:34.910
Please take this pikasha to the castle town.

08:34.910 --> 08:37.480
Those fluffy feathers look so comfy...

08:37.480 --> 08:38.920
I'm jealous.

08:38.920 --> 08:41.240
But we don't get to ride it, right?

08:42.570 --> 08:44.510
<i>I'll just try to ignore it...</i>

08:44.910 --> 08:46.640
Okay, thanks.

08:46.640 --> 08:48.180
Pikasha, thanks for the ride!

08:53.250 --> 08:55.340
It sure is fluffy!

09:02.070 --> 09:05.680
The pikasha put up a barrier 
to block the wind?

09:05.990 --> 09:08.330
It's not as windy as I thought it would be.

09:08.820 --> 09:12.600
Flying up here feels like something 
out of a real fantasy story!

09:13.040 --> 09:14.770
Is that the city?

09:33.830 --> 09:35.570
I'm almost there.

09:51.980 --> 09:53.360
Welcome!

09:54.970 --> 09:59.770
I thank you for the warm 
welcome, Your Majesty.

10:00.970 --> 10:03.210
<i>She looks relieved.</i>

10:03.210 --> 10:06.770
<i>She knows I'm not going to make 
fun of her in a place like this.</i>

10:07.360 --> 10:10.630
We've prepared a small parade.

10:11.390 --> 10:12.530
A parade?

10:13.180 --> 10:15.080
You're the star!

10:22.030 --> 10:23.640
I hope you all enjoy it, as well!

10:43.960 --> 10:46.690
<i>I don't like being the center of attention,</i>

10:46.690 --> 10:49.480
<i>but it'd be a waste of time to 
refuse and get in a fight...</i>

10:53.820 --> 10:56.350
<i>And I'm not hating it as 
much as I thought I would.</i>

11:04.730 --> 11:12.330
<i>Even if it's a game, only a few players will 
ever get to experience something like this!</i>

11:12.870 --> 11:16.140
<i>And that's why I should try to 
have as much fun as possible.</i>

11:18.010 --> 11:21.070
<i>This fantasy isn't reality.</i>

11:22.080 --> 11:25.580
<i>But the memories it'll leave are real!</i>

11:29.560 --> 11:31.720
I thank you for the warm welcome.

11:32.250 --> 11:37.130
But I think you went a little overboard...

11:37.130 --> 11:42.670
The point of the parade was 
to make sure every fairy

11:42.670 --> 11:45.550
in the kingdom knew you were here.

11:45.550 --> 11:50.120
They've all been waiting for you!

11:52.630 --> 11:56.900
There were even rumors I was 
keeping you all to myself.

11:58.160 --> 11:59.970
<i>Those rumors were true.</i>

12:03.640 --> 12:04.420
<i>Uh-oh!</i>

12:13.120 --> 12:15.660
Maybe I will keep you all to myself!

12:15.660 --> 12:17.090
<i>Hey!</i>

12:18.070 --> 12:20.480
Your Highness, control yourself.

12:20.940 --> 12:26.520
Of course. We'd appreciate it if you
 would stay in our country for a while.

12:26.890 --> 12:32.320
We won't do anything to spoil your stay, 
like assigning an escort or a monitor.

12:33.610 --> 12:35.290
Very well.

12:35.290 --> 12:39.510
Starting tomorrow, I'll go back 
to being a normal adventurer.

12:40.060 --> 12:44.870
<i>I'll head back to the fort town 
and start looking around.</i>

12:45.680 --> 12:49.010
Then with this, our audience is concluded.

12:52.130 --> 12:55.620
<i>This was the longest I've 
ever been logged in.</i>

12:59.200 --> 13:03.170
<i>Time to log out and...</i>

13:05.610 --> 13:07.210
Where are you going?

13:07.210 --> 13:10.720
I was going to the inn to get some sleep.

13:11.530 --> 13:14.640
Then why don't we sleep next 
to each other in my bed?

13:22.660 --> 13:23.950
Hey!

13:27.140 --> 13:28.840
Jeez!

13:29.970 --> 13:33.490
<i>I jumped out the window like a thief!</i>

13:34.830 --> 13:39.070
<i>Actually, I do have the 
Benevolent Thief skill...</i>

13:41.360 --> 13:47.350
<i>After I left the castle, they gave me a 
ride to the south fort town on a pikasha.</i>

13:48.010 --> 13:50.590
<i>The reason I chose the south side...</i>

13:51.300 --> 13:54.190
<i>was that this was the 
furthest side from Nexia,</i>

13:54.190 --> 13:57.370
<i>so there were fewer players here.</i>

13:59.500 --> 14:03.710
Excuse me! I defeated 
those eight high rabbits!

14:05.080 --> 14:07.220
You defeated them already?

14:07.220 --> 14:09.850
I thought it would take several days.

14:09.850 --> 14:12.720
Oh, did you see any thiefbirds?

14:12.720 --> 14:13.980
I sure did!

14:14.370 --> 14:16.610
After I shot a high rabbit,

14:17.130 --> 14:20.340
one tried to steal my kill 
right in front of me!

14:20.840 --> 14:22.720
So I shot it down!

14:23.590 --> 14:25.670
You're a really good shot!

14:26.430 --> 14:29.320
By the way, is there someplace 
I can use to cook?

14:30.040 --> 14:32.600
Use the kitchen in the back.

14:32.810 --> 14:34.780
I'll pay you rent for it.

14:34.780 --> 14:37.610
How kind of you!

14:38.090 --> 14:41.830
<i>This is a tavern and quest 
giver in the middle of town.</i>

14:41.830 --> 14:44.030
<i>The second floor is an inn.</i>

14:44.450 --> 14:49.990
<i>I've decided to stay here for a while, 
making this my base while I do quests.</i>

14:50.840 --> 14:53.010
First, I'll add some simple seasonings

14:53.010 --> 14:55.780
so I can get a feel for 
what the meat tastes like.

15:01.470 --> 15:03.270
Yeah, it's good.

15:03.270 --> 15:07.600
Both fillets are thinly sliced, 
but you can really taste the meat.

15:07.600 --> 15:09.550
There's no gamy taste, either.

15:09.900 --> 15:13.820
Okay, I'll make a simple dish that 
really brings out the ingredients!

15:14.600 --> 15:21.520
<b>Thiefbird Kabob with Lido
Grilled thiefbird meat on a skewer with Lido vegetables.
Effects: Speed Boost (Medium) Score: 8</b>

15:14.910 --> 15:17.790
<i><i>I decided to see if I could use 
thiefbird meat to make kabobs,</i></i>

15:17.790 --> 15:20.180
<i>just like I did with rabbithorn.</i>

15:21.650 --> 15:33.070
<b>Rabbit Hamburg Steak
A Hamburg steak made with a mix of high rabbit and thiefbird meat.
Not at all similar to the Hamburg steak humans normally eat, but still not bad.
Score: 7</b>

15:21.720 --> 15:23.640
<i>And I tried one more dish:</i>

15:23.640 --> 15:28.990
<i>a mix of chopped up high rabbit meat with 
the leftover thiefbird, kneaded into a patty!</i>

15:28.990 --> 15:33.060
<i>It's the first time I've tried this, 
and it might be a little weird, but...</i>

15:34.860 --> 15:36.730
Time to dig in!

15:36.730 --> 15:38.590
<i>First, the kabobs!</i>

15:39.470 --> 15:43.130
<i>Yeah, I can taste more of 
the flavor with every bite!</i>

15:45.680 --> 15:47.550
<i>This isn't bad, either.</i>

15:48.050 --> 15:50.660
I thought I smelled something good!

15:51.960 --> 15:53.950
That looks good!

15:53.950 --> 15:56.630
Human cooking really is different.

15:56.630 --> 15:58.180
I'd love to try it!

15:58.180 --> 16:01.320
Um, if you're willing to pay...

16:01.320 --> 16:02.270
We are!

16:04.380 --> 16:07.820
These kabobs go so well with beer!

16:07.820 --> 16:11.980
Those obnoxious high rabbits 
ain't so tough now, huh?

16:11.980 --> 16:15.450
I didn't know thiefbirds were so good!

16:15.450 --> 16:17.080
Gimme another drink!

16:17.080 --> 16:19.240
Coming!

16:19.240 --> 16:24.530
<i>I didn't think I'd be cooking even 
after coming to the Fairy Kingdom.</i>

16:24.530 --> 16:26.000
<i>I guess it's okay, though.</i>

16:26.810 --> 16:31.350
<i>For the next several days, my play 
cycle consisted of doing quests,</i>

16:32.390 --> 16:34.650
<i>cooking what I killed,</i>

16:35.540 --> 16:40.360
<i>and then eating and drinking with everyone!</i>

16:40.360 --> 16:45.260
<i>I was having a ton of fun 
with all the fairies, but...</i>

16:45.260 --> 16:48.200
Ma'am, you need to hide Earth, now!

16:48.200 --> 16:51.360
The fort leader's stupid 
daughter is on her way here!

16:52.330 --> 16:53.420
Hurry!

16:53.420 --> 16:55.170
Earth, hide down there!

17:00.730 --> 17:04.840
I've heard there's a human 
here who cooks strange food.

17:05.540 --> 17:07.910
Bring him to me immediately.

17:08.510 --> 17:12.690
I need to give him a chance 
to work as my chef.

17:12.690 --> 17:15.170
<i>That's an incredibly arrogant 
way of putting it...</i>

17:15.460 --> 17:20.590
I'm sorry. He's already left.

17:21.370 --> 17:26.510
I know he was here a few days ago, at least.

17:26.900 --> 17:29.210
Has he truly left?

17:29.210 --> 17:31.500
Nothing good will come of hiding him.

17:31.500 --> 17:36.950
I know he wouldn't refuse 
a chance to cook for me.

17:36.950 --> 17:43.710
I told him that it was dangerous to leave 
without taking time to properly prepare,

17:43.710 --> 17:47.280
but he said he had urgent 
business in the east.

17:56.880 --> 17:58.240
The east, yes?

17:58.240 --> 17:58.960
Yes.

17:59.970 --> 18:00.880
I see.

18:01.110 --> 18:02.000
Hey!

18:02.000 --> 18:05.020
Get me information on every 
adventurer who headed east.

18:05.020 --> 18:12.240
No chef can be allowed to leave this city 
without cooking for me at least once!

18:12.240 --> 18:16.150
When you find him, 
capture him and bring him to me!

18:16.150 --> 18:17.100
Yes, ma'am!

18:20.690 --> 18:23.350
You, too. Call me if you learn anything.

18:23.350 --> 18:24.300
Of course.

18:29.310 --> 18:31.130
What's her problem?

18:31.130 --> 18:33.740
She's always that stupid, right?

18:34.240 --> 18:36.040
It's safe now, I think.

18:36.380 --> 18:40.040
That stupid girl has her 
eye on you now, huh?

18:40.040 --> 18:42.610
I'm sorry, Earth.

18:42.610 --> 18:44.090
This is my fault...

18:44.440 --> 18:47.350
You knew who I was?

18:47.350 --> 18:48.400
Yes.

18:48.400 --> 18:53.770
There's actually an order from the 
queen that even if we recognize you,

18:53.770 --> 18:55.780
we're not to say anything.

18:55.780 --> 18:57.360
I didn't know.

18:57.360 --> 19:01.850
And you didn't seem to want 
special treatment, either.

19:02.700 --> 19:07.290
That girl causes a lot of problems 
with her personality as it is.

19:07.290 --> 19:11.110
But her father runs the fort, 
so nobody can say anything.

19:11.110 --> 19:16.540
And he never punishes her for her 
selfishness, either. He spoils her.

19:16.540 --> 19:19.320
<i>Is that okay for him to 
run the fort this way?</i>

19:19.320 --> 19:22.730
<i>Nothing good comes of being 
cruel to your people.</i>

19:23.300 --> 19:25.990
I can't cause any more problems for you.

19:25.990 --> 19:27.140
I'll leave.

19:33.340 --> 19:37.540
If it weren't for this, I would've 
wanted you to stay here forever.

19:37.540 --> 19:40.450
No, I had a great time.

19:40.860 --> 19:42.110
And...

19:43.020 --> 19:45.900
Having people say they liked my cooking,

19:45.900 --> 19:48.510
drinking with me and having fun...

19:48.950 --> 19:52.630
My life was lots of fun!

19:58.950 --> 20:01.430
<i>I waited for nightfall and then left.</i>

20:21.990 --> 20:23.610
You're Earth, yes?

20:24.420 --> 20:26.350
We've heard what's going on.

20:26.350 --> 20:29.910
That stupid girl has caused 
far too many problems.

20:30.350 --> 20:34.510
People are gathering evidence of 
her behavior to take to the queen.

20:35.080 --> 20:37.440
Come back when things calm down.

20:41.360 --> 20:43.900
Through here. Hurry.

20:43.900 --> 20:45.030
Thank you.

20:48.840 --> 20:50.020
This way.

20:52.180 --> 20:53.680
You're late.

20:55.260 --> 20:57.520
Hurry and get on my back.

21:00.800 --> 21:03.370
Your cooking was delicious.

21:05.680 --> 21:07.210
You ate it?

21:07.210 --> 21:10.230
Yes. And as a small way of saying thanks,

21:10.230 --> 21:12.450
I'll take you to the south town.

21:15.580 --> 21:17.360
Okay, then hurry!

21:17.360 --> 21:18.200
Leave it to me!

21:19.330 --> 21:22.210
<i>Farewell, fort town of the south!</i>

21:22.760 --> 21:25.750
Farewell, fairies of the south!

21:37.380 --> 21:39.140
We have received a report

21:39.870 --> 21:46.200
from the people of the south fort town 
that the daughter of the fort's leader

21:46.200 --> 21:49.160
exhibited inappropriate behavior
 toward a human adventurer yesterday.

21:50.320 --> 21:52.040
That's terrible...

21:52.040 --> 21:57.240
We're trying to be friends with the humans. 
Nothing can be allowed to stop that.

21:57.240 --> 22:02.490
And that adventurer... was Earth.

22:07.470 --> 22:09.930
<b>To Be Continued</b>
